00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.440
because you did not record data in the correct way, and then it's a

70
00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.960
bit of a process: okay, what can we do now to make sure that we either,

71
00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.120
if possible, retrospectively fill in the data gaps, or if not, from now

72
00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.040
on, for the future, we start to record the correct data, time stamps

73
00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.040
and whatever we needed to run cohort analysis.

74
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.479
So, it's a bit of a process.

75
00:04:54.479 --> 00:04:57.759
Make sure you get the basics right in terms of data access and

76
00:04:57.759 --> 00:04:59.430
kind of database location.

77
00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.720
Make sure that the people who have access to this data have their

78
00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:10.240
